    {
      "id": 27,
      "title": "",
      "viz": "text",
      "grid": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 12
      },
      "content": "<div style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: var(--text-color, #333); background-color: var(--bg-color, #fafafa); padding: 12px; line-height: 1.6;\">\n    \n    <h4 style=\"color: var(--heading-color, #4db6ac); margin-bottom: 10px;\">What this chart shows:</h4>\n    This chart visualizes the <span style=\"color: var(--highlight-color, #81c784); font-weight:bold;\">cumulative execution percentage</span> of test cases over time for each <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Regression test cycle</span>. \n    It helps track progress hour by hour, showing how quickly each cycle is approaching completion.\n\n    <ul style=\"margin-left: 20px;\">\n        <li><strong>Time Axis:</strong> Represents hourly intervals during the regression cycle.</li>\n        <li><strong>Value:</strong> Percentage of executed tests compared to total planned tests.</li>\n        <li><strong>Series:</strong> Each line represents a different test cycle.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h4 style=\"color: var(--heading-color, #4db6ac); margin-bottom: 10px;\">Why it matters:</h4>\n    <ul style=\"margin-left: 20px;\">\n        <li>Shows real-time progress and cumulative execution trends.</li>\n        <li>Helps identify cycles that are lagging behind or progressing well.</li>\n        <li>Higher percentages indicate faster execution and better adherence to timelines.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h4 style=\"color: var(--heading-color, #4db6ac); margin-bottom: 10px;\">How to interpret:</h4>\n    <ul style=\"margin-left: 20px;\">\n        <li>A steady upward trend means consistent progress toward completion.</li>\n        <li>Flat lines indicate no execution activity during that time window.</li>\n        <li>Example: If Cycle A reaches 80% by mid-day, it means most tests are executed and the cycle is close to completion.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <p style=\"color: var(--alert-color, #e57373); font-style:italic;\">&#9654; SCROLL Legends to find missing cycles and set time range on the dashboard level to explore detailed time intervals.</p>\n</div>",
      "mode": "html"
    },
